{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277108-world-of-darkness-tv-show-would-you-like-it","id":277108,"title":"World of Darkness TV Show: Would you like it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-10T05:15:38-07:00","id":277108,"title":"World of Darkness TV Show: Would you like it?","content":"With the wave of 20 Years books i been thinking about Kindred The Embraced and how TV shows have evolved. Doctor Who, Breaking Bad, Game of Thrones etc...<br /> If you were up to make a WoD tv show (based on the 20 years books or in games) What would you make? how would you make it?<br /> <br /> Personally, i would make an anthology series with intertwinned stories.<br /> The first one being of a neonate joining the camarilla in California<br /> second season i would use the Werewolfs for a season set on Nevada<br /> Third: Wraith (maybe the story of one of the background characters on season one or two and how this events have affected the wraiths)<br /> Fourth: Mage The Ascension , entering the Technocracy and how some characters (or background chars) have been operatives within the Union keeping track on the main characters and ending the season with &quot;He Has Awoken.&quot;<br /> Fifth: Start with the death of Ravnos and go with the Demons arriving to LA and how the vampires react to this.<br /> Sixth: a short story showing how some humans have been afected by the previous events and their introduction to Hunter Net, killing some of the main characters and yet getting ready to Inherit The Earth..<br /> Final Season: Armageddon/Gehhena/Apocalypse/Ascension/Cats and Dogs Living Togeather, its the end of the World baby!.<br /> <br /> and each season would have one cameo or two of signature characters (Beckett, Theo Bell / Laughing manyskins, Stuart stalks the truth/ Erik, Carpenter / Gaviel and Ahrimal / God45 and Cabbie22)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 10-10-2014, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T12:24:09-07:00","id":277481,"title":"","content":"I would divorce any show from metaplot and instead focus on personal horror. Make it local and personal for characters involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T19:37:18-07:00","id":278537,"title":"","content":"Sets for your seasons.<br /> Third: New Orleans or Springfield.<br /> Fourth: Las Vegas or Seattle.<br /> Fifth: (Changeling) New York or Miami.<br /> Sixth: (Hunter) Any of the previous cities.<br /> Seventh: (Mummy) Washington or Cairo.<br /> Eighth: (Kuei-Jin) Tokyo.<br /> Ninth: (Demon) per your suggestion, with the others joining in.<br /> Final: End of the World.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T05:45:00-07:00","id":278764,"title":"","content":"I think I watched for 3 eps the last time there was a WoD TV show. The vampires walking in sunlight just ruined it for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T12:53:30-07:00","id":278977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sidious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277108-world-of-darkness-tv-show-would-you-like-it?p=278764#post278764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I watched for 3 eps the last time there was a WoD TV show. The vampires walking in sunlight just ruined it for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be Kindred: the Embraced, aka Vampire: the Masquerade with just about everything good and interesting about it watered down or gutted out.<br /> <br /> But it was still better than Twilight...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T09:49:55-07:00","id":283928,"title":"","content":"I think it was called &quot;True Blood&quot;.<br /> <br /> While I enjoyed the show, every few episodes I would say &quot;there's another thing they ripped off of VtM&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T11:49:16-07:00","id":284004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277108-world-of-darkness-tv-show-would-you-like-it?p=278977#post278977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be Kindred: the Embraced, aka Vampire: the Masquerade with just about everything good and interesting about it watered down or gutted out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also known derisively as &quot;Vampire 90210&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it was still better than Twilight... </div> </div> </div>That's not saying much, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T13:03:03-07:00","id":284075,"title":"","content":"I would kill for a cWoD TV series. But, I would want Vampire: the Dark Ages and would expect some changes here or there. I think it'd be rather interesting, with the current trend for historical shows. It would also differentiate it from, say, Trueblood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T15:02:09-07:00","id":284252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277108-world-of-darkness-tv-show-would-you-like-it?p=284075#post284075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would kill for a cWoD TV series. But, I would want Vampire: the Dark Ages and would expect some changes here or there. I think it'd be rather interesting, with the current trend for historical shows. It would also differentiate it from, say, Trueblood.</div> </div> </div> </div>They would have to work pretty hard to keep it from being a straight True Blood/GoT mashup... actually, that sounds alright. But as long as we are daydreaming, less focus on sex n' bewbs and whatnot would be good. Most vampires use lust as a tool, and I am tired of seeing the undead as hypersexual love-making machines, rather than intelligent predators that use human sexuality as a weapon to secure prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T15:05:36-07:00","id":284258,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd go for that. I'd like a focus on vampires as less sex symbols, than as predators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T21:03:29-07:00","id":284587,"title":"","content":"Looks like most people here have said it. <br /> <br /> A WOD show would have to stay away from the &quot;TrueBlood&quot; style or making the vampires hyper-sexualized. Granted , seeing all the clans and there abilities would be awesome, and make the viewers realize that vampires have &quot;Layers&quot; of character and various appearances, besides &quot;Prettyboy- Bloodsucker&quot;. What would worry me is the settings maybe too dark for general viewing audiences.... especially when we get the <i> Tzimisce </i>involved. Certainly would be on more HBO styled channels, than general cable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T21:47:02-07:00","id":284627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277108-world-of-darkness-tv-show-would-you-like-it?p=284258#post284258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'd go for that. I'd like a focus on vampires as less sex symbols, than as predators.</div> </div> </div> </div>By baseline assumption, they're both. That's what makes them horrifyingly creepy - the feeding act is sex, and they take it from people that don't usually want it. Someone once summed it up even more succintly than in the past - they're barely metaphorical metaphors for rape and general abusive relationships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T21:57:21-07:00","id":284637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277108-world-of-darkness-tv-show-would-you-like-it?p=284627#post284627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By baseline assumption, they're both. That's what makes them horrifyingly creepy - the feeding act is sex, and they take it from people that don't usually want it. Someone once summed it up even more succintly than in the past - they're barely metaphorical metaphors for rape and general abusive relationships.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, but they are best used as metaphors- which is why I feel like a lot of modern portrayals of vampires completely miss the point. There is little need for the undead to rut like rabbits when the vampire is already equipped with its own representation of subversive non-consensual sex, i.e, feeding/embracing. Wanting to bone the vampire should be like wanting to get mauled by a werewolf or gnawed on by a zombie. It shouldn't be widely presented as cool or hot or sexy. You are giving in to the very danger the monster represents!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T22:03:40-07:00","id":284644,"title":"","content":"Vampires-as-Rape-Metaphors is an old interpretation, but by no means the only, or first. They can represent disease, corruption, and things gone wrong. They take, yes, but it's more than that. However, some Clans are based off that aspect of vampirism, and I think that it's worthwhile to explore that, with say, a Toreador. Give us the clans, highlight what makes them distinct, and important. Viewers will eat that up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T06:02:56-07:00","id":284892,"title":"","content":"As far as I know the classic vampire doesn't have a heart beat. So the sex thing was always an illusion. And the banging away like rabbit mating season has always been some silly Goth romance fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T22:23:52-07:00","id":285699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277108-world-of-darkness-tv-show-would-you-like-it?p=284644#post284644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires-as-Rape-Metaphors is an old interpretation, but by no means the only, or first. They can represent disease, corruption, and things gone wrong. They take, yes, but it's more than that. However, some Clans are based off that aspect of vampirism, and I think that it's worthwhile to explore that, with say, a Toreador. Give us the clans, highlight what makes them distinct, and important. Viewers will eat that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every vampire that isn't Giovanni, Nagaraja or other examples or horrendous maulers with deadly bites inflicts The Kiss. Hence, the vast, overwhelming majority of VTM-style vampires are going to fall under the Rape Metaphor Vampire envelope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T10:09:23-07:00","id":285991,"title":"","content":"WoD TV Casting Couch<br /> <br /> Vampire: Lance Henrikson (Venture), Sam Niel (Giovanni), Eiza Gonzalez (Toreador), Elisa Henson (Tremere)<br /> Werewolf: Brian Thompson (Shadow Lord), Richard Ayoade (Glass Walker), Doug Walker (Bone Gnawer), Alison Preglier (Black Fury)<br /> Mage: James Rolfe (Son of Ether), Jeremy Irons (Order of Hermes), Mila Kuniz (Verbena), Catherine Zeta-Jones (Virtual Adept)<br /> Wraith: Kelsey Grammer (Usurer), Micheal Keaton (Haunter), Emily Deschanel (Monitor), Melissa George (Sandman)<br /> Changeling: Tony Todd (Red Cap), Danny Huston (Troll), Christina Richi (Sluagh), Anjelica Huston (Pooka)<br /> Hunter: Gary Oldman (Defender), Nathan Fillion (Avenger), Laura Prepon (Redeemer), Gillian Anderson (Hermit)<br /> Mummy: Rachel Weisz (Khri-Habi), Arnold Vosloo (Mesektet), Jeffery Dean Morgan (Udja-sen), Alona Tal (Sefekhi)<br /> Demon: Doug Bradley (Defiler), Brad Pitt (Fiend), Marcia Gay Harden (Devil), Kate Blanchet (Malefactor)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T18:21:49-07:00","id":288118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277108-world-of-darkness-tv-show-would-you-like-it?p=278537#post278537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sets for your seasons.<br /> Third: New Orleans or Springfield.<br /> Fourth: Las Vegas or Seattle.<br /> Fifth: (Changeling) New York or Miami.<br /> Sixth: (Hunter) Any of the previous cities.<br /> Seventh: (Mummy) Washington or Cairo.<br /> Eighth: (Kuei-Jin) Tokyo.<br /> Ninth: (Demon) per your suggestion, with the others joining in.<br /> Final: End of the World.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be interesting. Do it in the style of American Horror Story, with every season being a different story and different characters. First season could be vampire, then werewolf, then mage, etc... You could go through all the various game lines this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T21:36:52-07:00","id":288243,"title":"","content":"I like it. But that would mean using the same actors though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T05:00:45-07:00","id":288457,"title":"","content":"i would re use some characters on each season.<br /> The first season would have a mysterious guy only known by the prince of the city (and some minor characters) who they call &quot;Mr World&quot; (Reference to American Gods), the second season (dealing with pentex) i would have Mr World and a woman &quot;The High Roller&quot; keepin in tabs with pentex.<br /> The third season, maybe show Mr World in a cameo<br /> fourth season: it would be revealed that Mr World is a NWO operative and that &quot;The High Roller&quot; its a Syndicate operative.<br /> fifth season: i would take the survivors of the first season (vampires) doing small cameos or even being antagonic forces with the demons<br /> Sixth: The hunters doing wiping jobs and cleaning jobs with some of the survivors of the previous seasons.<br /> <br /> ok..you know what? i got excited by this proposal... english aint my first language but...with the blessing of some of the admins, anyone wanna help me out (since english isnt my first language and my vampire lore is still in diapers) and writte down a pilot?!<br /> <br /> ok, ill try to contact rich and the others to see if they would be ok with me to writte down a script for a posible pilot if they ever wish to work something WoD related for TV. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 10-21-2014, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T11:02:20-07:00","id":289730,"title":"","content":"Awesome. Let's see.<br /> <br /> <i>My name is unimportant. It has been a long time since I have heard it myself. Some call me God, others Satan, some say Cain, and some say Charon. If you wish to call me something, call me Mr. World. Most of you live in a world where the only things certain is death and taxes. A world where the only monsters are on the media, those who prey on the weak and spread hate. A world where the light of the sun and streetlights reign supreme and keep things safe. Forget what you already know about the light, what you believe is reality. Come to the world my children inhabit, the true word A World of Darkness.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T12:25:15-07:00","id":291489,"title":"","content":"My purposed Characters for Season 1.<br /> <br /> Neonate - Jessica Antwiler - Newly Embraced Vampire of unknown origin (currently Caitiff, possibly Toreador, Ravnos, or Follower of Set). She is seeking the one who Sired her, she also has a burn on her right hand for trying to experiment if she was the traditional vampire or those who &quot;sparkle&quot;.<br /> <br /> Prince - Travis Copley - Clan Toreador - To him there is no other Clan who is best sooted to run the Kindred of LA than Toreador. He's a secret board member to most movie studios both major and independent, and he likes to run the city like a set of a film.<br /> <br /> Primogens - Rosemaria Briceno - Clan Toreador - Eiza Gonzalez - Started as a famous painter and now currently running 85% of LA's art museums. Rosemaria is Travis's right hand girl. Smart, precious, and deadly.<br /> <br /> Sir Brandon Neeson - Clan Ventrue - Lance Henrikson (pending, alternate casting choice Christopher Lambert) - Combine old money Hampton and Prohibition Era Chicago, that is Sir Neeson in a nutshell. Able to hide money where you need it without anybody noticing or enforce the Traditions with the same ruthlessness as Al Capone. While most would address most Primogen, but all who address Brandon Neeson it is always Sir, nobody knows why but when he is asked to perform Final Death on an guilty Kindred then you'll see why.<br /> <br /> Elizabeth O' Fallon - Clan Tremere - Elisa Hensen (pending) - Studious and a scholar. Owner of a few occult shops. She advises the Prince when events happen with supernatural influence or the mundane can't explain. Although she doesn't wish it, she is the Emissary for L.A.'s Magi.<br /> <br /> Icon - Clan Nosferatu - (casting pending) - L.A.'s Archivist. Once a leading actor who delves into historical records; for research for roles and for a fun hobby. He became arrogant with his fame his fame, almost like a tyrant on set. He insulted the Prince for cutting his pay. The Prince sent the previous Primogen to Embrace him. Renamed Icon for his former fame he worked his way up to the Primogen seat, to regain the Prince's trust and to keep an sharp eye on him.<br /> <br /> Maximilian Giovanni - Clan Giovanni - Sam Neil - A rarity for the Camarilla, a prominent medical entrepreneur with a few secrets beyond the grave. The more independent of the Primogens, representing the Camarilla to the Anarchs and viseversa, as well as representing the dead. One of the most powerful Kindred in L.A. next to the Prince.<br /> <br /> Dr. Tina Galazra - Clan Malkavian - (casting pending) - A psychiatrist gone off the deep end thanks to the Embrace. After being Embraced she stepped down from practicing to research, still on call just in case. The research lab lab is manned by seven ghouls during the day and three at night assisting her. Her research is on the bit of fringe and controversial. She is looking into the connection between blood born diseases and the human psyche. Both the Prince and Icon are keeping an close eye on her since her work is getting close to a possible Masquerade breech.<br /> <br /> Sheriff -<br /> Pedro Santinni - Clan Gangrel - (casting pending) - A wild streak that anyone would swear he is Lupine Kinfolk. The go to for the Prince and Maximilian to enforce the Traditions. Cunning and savage, there is almost nothing he will do to bring his target to justice. Icon is starting to suspect that Pedro might be a Sabbat infiltrator, even the Anarchs aren't as savage as this Gangrel.<br /> <br /> Debra Van Brunt - Clan Brujah - (casting pending) - The modern day Valkyrie. She uses the techniques of old with the tools of today. She is the go to for Icon, believing she is the perfect counter to the Gangrel. A fiery temper and sassy to boot. She keeps an eye on the gangs, taking a cut from drug trafficing. However whenever a gang in her territory disregards her rules. That gang ends up arrested with all the evidence pointing to them alone.<br /> <br /> Harry &quot;The Fixer&quot; Oranos - Clan Tzimisci Antitribu - (casting pending) - A former member of the Sabbat, though it wasn't for very long after being rescued by Sir Brandon Neeson. Another from Old Chicago, he remains under the employ of Sir Neeson. He takes care of the problems that Sir Neeson isn't able to ake care of himself either too busy or his Clan's nature wouldn't allow. While Icon knows about him, but he knows that Neeson's Fixer is faithfully loyal to the Camarilla. The Fixer is the secret weapon of not only Sir Neeson but also the Camarilla as well. Even the Anarchs and Sabbat knows not to mess with the Camarilla without earning the wrath of The Fixer.<br /> <br /> Sire plot line will be the next post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":1442,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","user":"PaladinDemo","date":". 10-27-2014, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T20:25:22-07:00","id":292626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/277108-world-of-darkness-tv-show-would-you-like-it?p=284892#post284892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know the classic vampire doesn't have a heart beat. So the sex thing was always an illusion. And the banging away like rabbit mating season has always been some silly Goth romance fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dhampir\" target=\"_blank\">Really</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T09:52:36-07:00","id":293817,"title":"","content":"Characters for Sire plot line. Here's the options.<br /> <br /> Dr. Gabriel Vondrak - Follower of Set - (casting pending) - Another rarity of the Camarilla. Dr. Vondrak is a Primogen from the city of Springfield. He was asked to visit L.A. after learning that the neonate has uncontrolled manifestations of Serpentis and the fact the burn on her hand haven't healed over time even with the assistance of blood. He shows her the Ways of Set without earning the wrath of the Camarilla. As they work together he adopts her as his childe. When it is time for him to return to his city, he offers her to join him so she can continue her training or let her stay in L.A. and continue practicing the Ways of Set.<br /> <br /> Sebastian Reynauld - Clan Toreador Antitribu - (casting pending) - A Sabbat through and through, his &quot;art&quot; is the crime scenes he leaves behind. And in true Sabbat fashion he Embraced the neonate and left her to fend for herself. Upon learning about her survival and her growing powers, he returns to reclaim his child and to show her the ways of the Sabbat. And to show her more extremes that the Toreador should be doing instead of what they like to &quot;limits themselves.&quot; He is unafraid of the Sheriffs, especially the Fixer and his Old Chicago mob boss Sir Neeson. He knows how to get around L.A. without getting noticed, even with Icon's consent vigil.<br /> <br /> Constanta Cozma - Clan Ravnos - (casting pending) - She lives in constant regret for leaving her childe behind. Her small family was forced to pull stakes during a conflict between the Anarchs and Sabbat. Though the incident was managed by the Camarilla as a favor to the Anarchs to keep the mortals in the dark, the Ravnos family felt that it was time to go if the fight has gone out of hand. Constanta has returned to reclaim her childe she left behind, though the neonate is cautious since Constanta is will evacuate at the first sign of trouble. Would Constanta leave her behind again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T15:32:39-07:00","id":299387,"title":"","content":"You know what would be good, for a amateur producer too make a small fan-film that could blow people away, much like how Street Fighter had with it's live action series, Assassin's Fist did. I wonder how CCP would respond to that. It'd obviously be non-profit fan-film, but those can jump start at least web series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T11:01:05-08:00","id":300206,"title":"","content":"One problem is that Me and Crowley are probably half a world away (which reminds me I need to hop on Skype). Second would be conflicting locations. My hometown has quite a bit of churches and cemeteries so it would be better suited for Wraith or Demon. It'll be a great way to pitch the series, but there will be a few conflicting issues (locations, scheduling, props, actors, setting, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T00:00:38-08:00","id":307936,"title":"","content":"Here's what I got for the opening scenes for the pilot.<br /> <br /> <i> Jessica awakens to a bloody hotel room. Beams of sunlight leaking through cracks between aluminum foil and curtains as the sun sets indicating from the low hues. She opens a compact to use the mirror within. Looking in the mirror she sees that her skin is paler, blood covering her mouth, and her canines are sharper.</i><i> She stares in shock at the reflection, throwing the compact across the room, it slams against the wall</i>, <i>popping open and the makeup shattering, the chunks scattering everywhere. She looks towards the beams of light, raising her right hand as she steps towards the light, hoping it is not true, or she might be those other types that sparkle. As soon as the back of her right hand touches the light, smoke sprang forth and sering pain shoots through her body, she recoils in fear and pain. Retreating to the bathroom to get water on the wound, throwing both hot and cold water in a blinding motion. As she soaks the wound, she discovers a dead body in the bathtub. With a series of bites on the neck, limbs, and two on the exposed torso, along with semi fresh blood as if the body was &quot;stewing&quot;.<br /> Hunger courses through her mind, blocking out the pain. She scampers over to the tub, almost fascinated by the blood. Her head plunges into the tub, lapping up blood off the bottom like a pet drinking water for the first time after a few days. The door of the main room shatters open. She stops and turns to the bathroom door when two figures enter the bathroom.<br /> The first a hideous creature, warped skull, short wiggling tendrils for &quot;hair&quot;, alien looking eyes, fearsome fangs and claws. &quot;In here Sir.&quot; It said into the door way. The second emerging, recognizingly human, in a full Armoni suit, a trench coat and fedora not only well worn but also purposely mismatched with the suit. &quot;Good job son.&quot; He said in almost a accent that seemed to come from an old Noir movie. In fact both seem to have similar accents and styles.</i><br /> <i>&quot;It's alright sweetheart. Yer safe now. The name's Brandon, and this is my right hand Harry.&quot; The mobster said as he extended his hand to help Jessica up. Still shaken at the sight of &quot;Harry&quot;, she gradually takes Brandon's hand.<br /> Brandon helps Jessica up gently, like a police officer would for a frightened child. &quot;Bag the blood for the young lady, standard clean up, Crip hit.&quot; He says to the thing he called Harry. Jessica would have sworn Brandon would have said broad considering their look and accents, but she was more confused with what he meant by standard clean up and Crip hit. Is this mobster starting a gang war? Brandon leads Jessica out of the hotel room, once she was outside she sees that it is twilight, lots of purple hues as the night descended.<br /> &quot;I'm afraid to say this sweetheart, but you are no longer human.&quot; Brandon says as he pulls out a cigar and a matchbook from his trench coat. &quot;We're what you call Vampires. And no it's not the laughing stocks that the young people like these nights.&quot; He cuts the end off the cigar with what looked like a claw before he places itin his mouth and lighting it with a match. Jessica flinches at the sight of the flame as Brandon lit the cigar.<br /> &quot;Yes, fire hurts us, along with the sun and other stuff. But don't call us weak. Our strength is the blood, it is our food, currency, power, and greatest weapon.&quot; Brandon says as he takes a long puff on the cigar as he starts leading the way to the stairwell. Jessica follows closely behind like a lost puppy.<br /> The two walk down the stairs to the ground when a large crash erupts from the room as Harry walked out with a blood bag about a quarter full. Brandon points to Harry as Jessica looks to where Brandon is pointing to. She watches almost in terror as Harry jumps from the second story floor and land on the ground without any injury, almost like a perfect landing from the Olympics.<br /> &quot;That is one of many tricks we can use, though you shouldn't do some of our tricks in front of the mortals.&quot; He says as Harry rejoins Brandon and Jessica, with Jessica backing up a foot. &quot;And not all of us are as good looking as my old friend here.&quot; He says with a bit of a chuckle. Harry with a chuckle of his own, &quot;Good one Sir.&quot;<br /> Brandon and Harry leads the way to a limo parked several yards away from the motel. Harry opens the door for Brandon as he enters the limo. He assists Jessica into the limo gently. Harry hands Brandon the blood bag then closes the door. Brandon hands Jessica the blood bag as another car door opens and closes. The limo starts and begins to move as Brandon takes another heavy puff off the cigar.<br /> &quot;What's your Clan young lady?&quot; Brandon asks looking at Jessica trying to start a conversation. &quot;What?&quot; Jessica replies</i><i> at last, the first time in quite a while. Brandon gives a curious look, &quot;Your Clan, your family to put it loosely.&quot; &quot;I have no idea.&quot; Jessica says, &quot;I just woke up and found the room covered with blood, the body in the tub, you and your... um... friend. Other than that I just found out that I'm a Vampire, that's </i><i>all I know.&quot; &quot;I see.&quot; Brandon says, &quot; To make things short, Vampires are descended from the first, Caine. There are thirteen different kinds which are called Clans. Think of the Clans as a dysfunctional family.&quot; He takes another puff of the cigar. &quot;Each Clan has their own traits, abilities, and weaknesses on top of what we already got from Caine.&quot;<br /> </i><br /> <br /> To be continued.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":1442,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","user":"PaladinDemo","date":". 11-15-2014, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T13:07:09-08:00","id":308475,"title":"","content":"<i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i> would do well as a teen show as demonstrated by The Vampire Diaries/The Originals and Teen Wolf. The difference would of course be that there'd be way more politics already baked into the setting, and the characters would only be able to bang one another in secret, and at great cost to themselves (unless of course they birth the perfect metis or some such thing)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}